    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Reunited in 1861 after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#bartolome-mitre">Bartolomé Mitre</a>’s victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#battle-of-pavon">Pavón</a>, under the federal Constitution of 1853 as amended in 1860.</li><li>Mass European immigration and exports of beef and grain made it one of the world’s richest countries by 1914.</li><li>From 1930 coups, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#peronism">Peronism</a> and economic crises alternated, until democracy returned in 1983 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#falklands-war">Falklands War</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In the national <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#census">census</a> of 1914 about 30 per cent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#argentina">Argentina</a>’s population had been born abroad, twice the share in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#united-states">United States</a> at the time.</p></aside>
    </section>

